// The two tilt windows a person meets, named in one place.
//
// `displayed` and `displayed_plain` are the range of the tilt figures read for a design
// (Compare's "Tilt average to ±90°", Baseline's Measure Tilt, the command line): the mean over the
// tilts up to the Preferences choice "Tilt Average Range" from table up, ±90° (every tilt) by
// default. Rust sets both words from the preference at start-up and on every change, on the main
// window and on every Compare window (`gui::preferences::register_tilt_range_sink`):
// `displayed` for captions ("to ±90°"), `displayed_plain` for sentences ("to 90°").
// `scored` is the window the scoring tools (Optimize, Trials, Angle Sweep, Retarget, Tune) average
// their tilt term over, always. It never follows the preference. Hints that name a window take the
// word from here.
export global TiltWindows {
    in property <string> displayed: "to ±90°";
    in property <string> displayed_plain: "to 90°";
    out property <string> scored: "±90°";
}
